% ============================================================================
% sound-properties.query.adj — a worked recall over the physics sound-properties
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does pitch
% correspond to physically?": it states no physics fact — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `sound_property` rows and returns the physical quantity + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% physical quantity `frequency`, recall the perceived property heard as it —
% pitch). A perceived word the source never maps — `rhythm` — is never sorted
% into a physical quantity, so a recall on it abstains honestly; the engine
% never invents a correspondence.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli sound-properties.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "sound-properties.adj"

? sound_property(pitch, $P)          % expect frequency
? sound_property(loudness, $P)       % expect amplitude
? sound_property(timbre, $P)         % expect waveform
? sound_property($X, frequency)      % expect pitch — reverse recall
? sound_property(rhythm, $P)         % expect abstain — the source never maps rhythm
